    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0668" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg568"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1508: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Technical Board</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-05T22:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1920—10
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 7—6:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Czech evacuation proceeding fairly well; all east of Harbin; hope to have them
                    all off Chinese Eastern in four days. Japanese control everything Nikolsk to
                    Vladivostok. … Heavy reenforcements Japanese army troops constantly arriving
                    Vladivostok and heavy movement their troops from Changchun to Harbin scheduled
                    to commence to-morrow in which case Russian railway men here threaten to strike
                    … Personally, I am carrying out Department’s <pb facs="0669" n="569"
                        xml:id="pg569"/> instructions to evacuate Service Corps and hope to close up
                    my matters shortly, resign from the Board and leave here as soon as
                    possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
